+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive coffee homepage with rewards enrollment using browser-assisted Email Verification (EVP). No OTP or magic link email is sent. Accounts are created only after server verification succeeds.
+
+Requires Node 24+. Install with `pnpm install`; check syntax with `pnpm build`; run isolated cryptographic tests with `pnpm test`. `pnpm start` runs the Node application when deployment is desired. The server serves the homepage and static assets as well as `POST /api/verify-email`; a static-only host cannot verify or create accounts.
+
+Configure `APP_ORIGIN` as the exact public HTTPS origin, `NODE_ENV=production`, and `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN` with a valid Chrome origin-trial token registered for that origin. Terminate HTTPS at your hosting proxy. See https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification for current browser/provider support and trial registration. The customer must use a participating browser/provider and be signed in to their provider in the same browser profile. Unsupported or failed verification displays retry guidance without creating an account or sending email.
+
+The native form includes `autocomplete="email"` and a hidden `autocomplete="email-verification-token"` input with a per-render cryptographic nonce. Native submission is intentional: the browser attaches the presentation at submission. Server-held session state is bound to an HttpOnly, SameSite cookie (Secure and `__Host-` on HTTPS) and consumed atomically before verification. Page responses use `Cache-Control: no-store`. The verifier checks DNS issuer delegation before discovery, public-only HTTPS discovery/JWKS destinations without redirects, issuer and holder signatures, email/verified claims, token freshness/expiry, audience, nonce, and SD-JWT hash binding. Missing issuer `kid` supports trial verification of all matching JWKS keys.
+
+SQLite stores members and short-lived verification sessions in `DATA_DIR` (default `./data`). Persist and protect this directory and run one Node process per database. Names and original email casing are preserved; email uniqueness is case-insensitive. Marketing consent is optional and stored separately. This implements enrollment only; future account sign-in and purchase/points integrations require separate work. No mail service, token logging, password collection, or inbox access is used.
+
+The server entrypoint is never imported by tests. Tests use locally generated issuer/holder keys and an injected key resolver; they do not start a server or contact real providers. Stock photos are hosted by Unsplash; fonts by Google Fonts.
